repository-code: "https://github.com/PJGriff26/materials-demand"
version: 3.0.0
date-released: 2026-05-12
license: MIT
keywords:
  - critical materials
  - Monte Carlo simulation
  - energy transition
  - material flow analysis
  - supply chain risk
  - NREL Standard Scenarios
abstract: >-
  This repository implements a stock-flow Monte Carlo simulation framework
  for estimating critical-material demand under the NREL Standard Scenarios
  2024 (10,000 iterations × 61 scenarios × 9 reporting years × 31 materials
  × 19 generation technologies). Material-intensity uncertainty is sampled
  from forced-lognormal distributions with tail validation and CV borrowing
  for small samples. Supply-chain risk is layered on top using OECD CRC
  weighting, USGS Mineral Commodity Summaries 2025 production and reserves,
  and US Census Bureau import-partner shares. The framework supports four
  cadence treatments for the 3-yr NREL reporting interval (default: PCHIP
  monotone cubic Hermite interpolation; Fritsch & Carlson 1980).
